{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_testing_verify_command", "label": "npm run verify", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 3-7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lint, build and tests with coverage thresholds; the single gate."}, {"id": "docs_testing_hermetic_policy", "label": "Hermetic test policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No network, no credentials, no external services. A git binary for the git transport tests is the only external dependency."}, {"id": "docs_testing_coverage_thresholds", "label": "Coverage thresholds as a floor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 211-215", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "80% lines, functions, branches and statements. Index files, type-only modules and test helpers are excluded because coverage of a re-export is noise. Coverage is a floor, not a goal; the tests that matter are the ones that would have caught a real defect."}, {"id": "docs_testing_mirrored_test_tree", "label": "test/ tree mirrors src/", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "test/core/mailbox.test.ts covers src/core/mailbox.ts; nothing under src/ is a test. Shared doubles live in test/core/testing.ts."}, {"id": "docs_testing_conformance_suite_per_transport", "label": "Transport conformance suite run per transport", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_testing_e2e_suite", "label": "End-to-end suite (two runtimes, real transport)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 23, 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The suite that answers \"does it work\": two independent runtimes against a shared directory, proxying real HTTP."}, {"id": "docs_testing_ciphertext_assertion", "label": "Cleartext-scan assertion over transport bytes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads every byte the transport ever held and asserts no application data, query string or exposure name appears in clear text. This is the executable form of the security model's encryption claim."}, {"id": "docs_testing_clock_injection", "label": "Injected Clock and TestClock.advance", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 31", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Time is injected everywhere so retry and backoff suites run in milliseconds. TestClock.advance drains the microtask queue through a macrotask boundary before each timer, which is what stops fake-timer tests hanging on deep promise chains."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_suite", "label": "Scenario suite", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 33-48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unit tests answer \"does this function behave\"; scenarios answer \"can a user do this, and is it stopped from what it should not\". Every bug in the 0.2.x series was invisible to the unit suite because it needed real processes, sockets, files and restarts."}, {"id": "docs_testing_can_cannot_rule", "label": "CAN/CANNOT pairing requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The runner fails a scenario declaring only one half, because a capability nobody has bounded is a capability nobody understands. The PASS CAN / PASS CANNOT lines are the documentation."}, {"id": "docs_testing_e2e_run_sh", "label": "e2e/run.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 37-48", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tiered runner (fast/live/all) with --npm, --only and --list; scenarios are one file per subject under e2e/fast and e2e/live with the harness in e2e/lib.sh, and the runner picks up new files automatically."}, {"id": "docs_testing_fast_tier", "label": "Fast tier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 50-66", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No network, no credentials, CI-safe, runs before every release, under four minutes. The slow files are the ones that must wait for real time: breakers tripping, peer restarts, a retention window."}, {"id": "docs_testing_live_tier", "label": "Live tier", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 68-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Real credentials and a real repository, about fifteen minutes; it writes a deaddrop-data branch and leaves it, so point it at a private throwaway. Explicitly not for CI."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_01_configuration", "label": "01-configuration.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bad configuration is refused out loud, before anything looks alive."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_02_control_plane", "label": "02-control-plane.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The control plane is an owner-only socket, and a data directory too deep for one still works."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_03_two_peers", "label": "03-two-peers.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Discovery, round trip, ciphertext on the transport, static exposure limits, offline redelivery, expiry, 30 MiB payloads and the 32 MiB cap."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_04_exposures", "label": "04-exposures.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 59", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "allowPeers, and an http exposure proxying a local server that is up and then down."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_05_broadcast", "label": "05-broadcast.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 60", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One publisher, three subscribers, one peer that never subscribed, one that was offline."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_06_key_rotation", "label": "06-key-rotation.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 52, 61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two-stage rotation with no downtime, and a peer left on the retired key failing closed. Slow because it restarts peers."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_07_failover", "label": "07-failover.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 52, 62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A transport dying under a running peer, recovery, and parallel vs failover placement policy. Slow because it waits for real circuit breakers to trip."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_08_git_transport", "label": "08-git-transport.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The git transport against a local bare repository, including two runtimes sharing one workDir."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_09_dashboard", "label": "09-dashboard.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dashboard binds where told, renders with no network, only reads, and starts no runtime."}, {"id": "docs_testing_scenario_10_reaping", "label": "10-reaping.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 52, 65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mail for a peer that comes back survives its window; mail for one that never existed is reclaimed, and running peers' beacons are not. Slow because it must outlast a retention window."}, {"id": "docs_testing_peer_id_collision", "label": "peerId collision trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 80-82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "peerId defaults to the hostname, so two runtimes on one box share a mailbox address, poll each other's mail and fail with DECODE_FAILED on garbage frames. Correct behaviour for a colliding address, and the first thing to check when a local multi-peer setup misbehaves."}, {"id": "docs_testing_manual_walkthrough", "label": "Two-machine manual walkthrough", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 88-181", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answers the one question the automated suite cannot: does this move real bytes between two real machines over a real GitHub repository. Half an hour, two machines with Node 20.11+, git and gh."}, {"id": "docs_testing_walkthrough_ciphertext_check", "label": "Walkthrough step 8: verify the transport cannot read traffic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 171-177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Clone the deaddrop-data branch and grep for a string from your HTTP response, expecting no matches. Stated as checking the security model's claim rather than trusting it."}, {"id": "docs_testing_round_trip_measurement", "label": "Measure the round trip to set requestTimeoutMs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 179, 194", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It will be seconds, not milliseconds, and that number is what requestTimeoutMs should come from."}, {"id": "docs_testing_git_push_exit_code_bug", "label": "git push exit-code bug found only live", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing local reproduced it because a local push is too fast to interleave. The standing argument for keeping the live tier."}, {"id": "docs_testing_manual_checklist", "label": "Manual verification checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 183-209", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GitHub live, scale and endurance, and platform sections. Anything ticked is recorded with the date and version tested."}, {"id": "docs_testing_platform_gaps", "label": "Platform gaps needing a human", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 84-86, 205-207", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows named pipes are unexercised (the Windows CI job proves the suite passes, not that anyone used the control plane there); SMB/NFS polling and atomic writes, and OneDrive/Dropbox partial-write corruption, need real hardware."}, {"id": "docs_testing_real_defects_caught", "label": "Three defects real tests caught", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 215", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The circuit breaker reading raw state instead of time-adjusted state, the mailbox acknowledging messages with no handler installed, and the topic reaper deleting messages whose age it could not determine. Each noted in the commit that fixed it."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_testing_verify_command", "target": "docs_testing_coverage_thresholds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 4, 213", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_testing_hermetic_policy", "target": "docs_testing_fast_tier", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "lines 9, 52", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_testing_e2e_suite", "target": "docs_testing_ciphertext_assertion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_testing_ciphertext_assertion", "target": "docs_security_model_encrypted_envelope", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/testing.md", "source_location": "line 29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_testing_walkthrough_ciphertext_check", "t